Subject: Add `--use-distinct-char32-t`, mirroring `--use-distinct-char16-t`

`char16_t` has had `--use-distinct-char16-t` since 0.60: the C++ type is its
own type rather than a typedef of an integer, Rust has no equivalent, and a
consumer which has to name the C++ type again needs something to name it with.
Everything in that argument is equally true of `char32_t`, which
`build_builtin_ty` collapses to `IntKind::U32` with no way to ask it not to.

This adds the arm the collapse is missing, along the same three seams the
`char16_t` support uses: an `IntKind::Char32` variant, a `CXType_Char32` arm in
`build_builtin_ty` guarded by the new option, and a codegen arm emitting the
fake type `bindgen_cchar32_t`. `Char32` is unsigned and four bytes wide by
[basic.fundamental]/9, so `is_signed` and `known_size` can answer for it rather
than deferring to a layout, as they already do for `Char16`.

Off by default, so no existing output changes.

--- a/codegen/helpers.rs
+++ b/codegen/helpers.rs
@@ -267,6 +267,9 @@
             // this case and do something special for C++ bindings
             // containing the C++ type char16_t.
             IntKind::Char16 => syn::parse_quote! { bindgen_cchar16_t },
+            // As `Char16`, and only reachable the same way: `char32_t` is
+            // collapsed to `u32` unless `use_distinct_char32_t` asks for it.
+            IntKind::Char32 => syn::parse_quote! { bindgen_cchar32_t },
             IntKind::SChar => raw_type(ctx, "c_schar"),
             IntKind::UChar => raw_type(ctx, "c_uchar"),
             IntKind::Short => raw_type(ctx, "c_short"),
--- a/ir/context.rs
+++ b/ir/context.rs
@@ -2023,6 +2023,9 @@
                 TypeKind::Int(IntKind::Char16)
             }
             CXType_Char16 => TypeKind::Int(IntKind::U16),
+            CXType_Char32 if self.options().use_distinct_char32_t => {
+                TypeKind::Int(IntKind::Char32)
+            }
             CXType_Char32 => TypeKind::Int(IntKind::U32),
             CXType_Long => TypeKind::Int(IntKind::Long),
             CXType_ULong => TypeKind::Int(IntKind::ULong),
